#: src/features/legal/texts/HowPowrDecides.tsx
msgid "Estimated 1-rep max and strength trends"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/legal/texts/HowPowrDecides.tsx
msgid "Every number POWR uses is a value in one versioned list, the rules registry. Each value names its evidence and its sources, so any suggestion can be traced back. Where research gives a clear answer, POWR uses it. Where research is thin, it uses an established coaching convention, and where neither gives a number, its own estimate, labelled as such."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/legal/texts/Privacy.tsx
msgid "Everything you enter is stored only on this device. We never receive it: there is no account, analytics or tracking. Only you can export it, as a backup file."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/legal/texts/HowPowrDecides.tsx
msgid "Exercise library and templates: {contentVersion}"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/legal/texts/HowPowrDecides.tsx
msgid "From the weight, reps and effort of your sets, POWR estimates the most you could lift once (your estimated 1-rep max). Heavy, hard sets count most. The trend is smoothed, because single sessions vary by several percent; a change is only called likely real once it is larger than that day-to-day variation and lasts for a few sessions."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/legal/texts/Privacy.tsx
msgid "Hosting"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/legal/texts/Privacy.tsx
msgid "If this notice changes in substance, POWR shows the new version and asks you to confirm it before you continue. The version is shown at the top of this page."
msgstr ""

